# CH22 — A Gate with Two Keys. Crown Heart: two teams, alternating locks, the Crown Vessel (B12), SC11.
# CH23 — Let the Names Remain. CH24 — The First Unborrowed Morning.

@scene D10_DOCK once
music M028
say narr | Lanternwake ties up at the Crown Heart - a rib of dragon bone and relay glass rising out of the Ember Sea.
say ivo | Two lungs. West runs the physical pressure; east runs the name-binding circuit. The locks alternate - west, east, west, east.
say oriel | Two teams, then. Four and four. Neither team can finish alone and neither can shut the other in.
say sable | The swap bells in each lung pass control between the teams whenever you like.
say narr | (This is the Accord Dock. You can still leave: Lanternwake is moored behind you. Past the Concord Bridge, the Crown Vessel.)
backup pre_finale
say narr | (A protected backup has been written: "Before the Final Descent". It is kept separate from your slots and from any clear save.)
objective oriel | When ready, use the split lever on the dock to divide into two teams.
@end

@scene D10_CREW
say pilot | Lanternwake's moored and not going anywhere without you. Rest, restock, come back whenever.
shop SHOP_SHIP
@end

@scene D10_SPLIT
if flag:d10_split already
say narr | Two teams of five. Same stores, same growth, same recovery point here. Anyone left over holds the recovery point.
split_party
set d10_split
say narr | (Team A takes the west lung; Team B the east. West first.)
team A
objective oriel | Team A: release the first west lock. Then ring the swap bell to hand over to Team B.
warp D10_R02 from_r01 left
end
label already
choice | Send Team A west -> a | Send Team B east -> b | Stay -> stay
label a
team A
warp D10_R02 from_r01 left
end
label b
team B
warp D10_R03 from_r01 right
label stay
@end

@scene D10_SWAP
if var:team_on>=2 toA
say narr | The swap bell. Its note carries through the bone to the other lung.
choice | Hand over to Team B (east) -> go | Stay -> stay
label go
team B
warp D10_R03 from_r01 right
end
label toA
say narr | The swap bell. Its note carries through the bone to the other lung.
choice | Hand over to Team A (west) -> go2 | Stay -> stay
label go2
team A
warp D10_R02 from_r01 left
label stay
@end

@scene D10_W1
if flag:d10_w1 done
sfx FX010
set d10_w1
say narr | The first west lock releases with a gasp of pressure. Across the Heart, something in the east lung unclamps.
objective oriel | West lock 1 released. Ring the swap bell - Team B's first lock is free.
end
label done
say narr | The first west lock is open.
@end

@scene D10_E1
if flag:d10_e1 done
if !flag:d10_w1 wait
sfx FX024
set d10_e1
say narr | The first east lock unbinds a ring of names from the circuit. They drift up like sparks. The west lung's second lock unclamps.
objective oriel | East lock 1 released. Swap to Team A for the second west lock.
end
label wait
say narr | The lock is held by the west lung's pressure. Team A has to release theirs first.
end
label done
say narr | The first east lock is open.
@end

@scene D10_W2
if flag:d10_w2 done
if !flag:d10_e1 wait
sfx FX010
set d10_w2
say narr | The second west lock opens. The pressure in the Heart drops to a long, slow exhale.
objective oriel | West lock 2 released. Swap to Team B for the last east lock.
end
label wait
say narr | This lock is still bound by the east circuit. Team B has to release their first lock.
end
label done
say narr | The second west lock is open.
@end

@scene D10_E2
if flag:d10_e2 done
if !flag:d10_w2 wait
sfx FX024
set d10_e2
set d10_done_lungs
say narr | The last east lock falls open. Both lungs breathe out together. The Concord Bridge unfolds from the dock.
team all
objective oriel | Both lungs are open. Meet on the Concord Bridge (north of the dock).
warp D10_R04 from_r01 up
end
label wait
say narr | This lock is still held by the west pressure. Team A has one more lock.
end
label done
say narr | The last east lock is open.
@end

@scene D10_REUNITE once
say narr | The two teams meet in the middle of the Concord Bridge.
say corren | Nobody fell.
say pip | Nobody forged anything. I checked.
say tessa | Everyone's tired. That's allowed.
say narr | (Rest at the lamp and choose the four who will face the Crown Vessel. The others will hold the release anchors from the bridge.)
formation
objective dain | Cross the Concord Bridge north to the Crown Vessel.
@end

@scene CH22_VESSEL once
music silence
say narr | The Crown Vessel: a heart of relay glass the size of a chapel, with a man's shape half-sunk in its surface.
still ST12_crown_heart
say voss | Order. You broke it. I am putting it back. Every fragment, every host, one voice.
say dain | You don't have a voice anymore, Voss. You have a command.
say voss | It is the same thing.
say oriel | It never was.
say narr | Behind the party, on the bridge, the others take up the release anchors. Across the Ember Sea, the towns begin the procedure at the same moment.
battle B12 noflee
set b12_done
music silence
say narr | The Vessel cracks from the inside. Voss's shape comes loose from the glass - a tired old man in a torn uniform, gasping.
say voss | ...They will not obey anyone now.
say sable | That was the point.
say narr | Soldiers from the accord take Voss down to the boats. He will be heard, too.
objective dain | Step out into the Open Sky.
@end

@scene CH22_SC11 once
music silence
say narr | The Open Sky. The last of the network drifts away as ordinary light. There are no chains in it.
say narr | Something like a door stands open beside Raven - a form of light and scale, restored and waiting.
say ilyr | The way is open.
say dain | I know.
say ilyr | You are not going to ask me to stay.
say dain | Would that make it easier?
say ilyr | No.
say dain | Then I will ask whether you wish to.
say ilyr | For now.
say dain | And when that changes?
say ilyr | We speak again.
say narr | The binding pattern on Raven's hands fades. What is left is a promise, not a lock - one either of them can end.
set voluntary_accord
chapter CH22
music M016
fade out 1.0
warp T07_MARKET from_hearth up
fade in 1.0
call CH23_WALK
@end

@scene CH23_WALK once
say narr | Hearthward, some weeks later.
say mara | Records are open. Engines run on waterwheels and wind. The rescue routes have names on them. It isn't finished.
say mara | It's started. That's what you get.
if flag:q01_done q1
goto q1b
label q1
say narr | At the market wall, the quarry workers' names are carved where their numbers were. Mara chose the inscription.
label q1b
say narr | Rook's hearing is held in the open, on the pontoons. Oni appears before the Whitebone survivors, as promised. Nobody is paraded. Everybody is heard.
say narr | Families light a lamp for each person lost. The lamps are not counted against anyone.
chapter CH23
objective dain | Walk Hearthward. When you're ready, go to the communal hearth.
@end

@scene CH23_EPILOGUES once
say narr | By the hearth, the crew talk about what comes next.
if flag:q02_done tessa2
say tessa | I'm going to teach. Short lessons. Nobody faints.
goto tessa_end
label tessa2
say tessa | The public workshop opens tomorrow. The apprentice's name goes above the door. Mine goes under it.
label tessa_end
epilogue C02
if flag:q03_done corren2
say corren | Rescue roster. Tuesdays. Some Thursdays.
goto corren_end
label corren2
say corren | The Returners' Wall has forty names now. Mine isn't one of them. That's how I like it.
label corren_end
epilogue C03
if flag:q04_done ivo2
say ivo | Lanternwake needs maintenance. So does everything else. Good.
goto ivo_end
label ivo2
say ivo | Every town has the notes now. Somebody in Bellharbor already improved the boiler. Didn't ask me. Perfect.
label ivo_end
epilogue C04
if flag:q05_done nera2
say nera | I'm drawing maps for anyone who asks. With the other guides' names on them.
goto nera_end
label nera2
say nera | Every public map has warnings, detours, and who to blame. I'm on three of them. Deservedly.
label nera_end
epilogue C05
if flag:q06_done oriel2
say oriel | Ordinary medicine. Slow, useful, asked for.
goto oriel_end
label oriel2
say oriel | The sanctuary asks first now. Always. My mistake is in the public record, where it belongs.
label oriel_end
epilogue C06
if flag:q07_done sable2
say sable | The hearing continues. I go back every month.
goto sable_end
label sable2
say sable | They asked me a question at the hearing. I answered it without qualification. The hearing continues.
label sable_end
epilogue C07
if flag:q08_done pip2
say pip | Blank forms, proper seal. Very boring. Very good.
goto pip_end
label pip2
say pip | The registry takes amendments now, and records who made each one. Including mine.
label pip_end
epilogue C08
if !recruited:C09 c09_end
if q:QC09 c092
say kitsune | The court has a regent and a mirror nobody is ordered to look into. I visit. I leave before the bowing starts.
goto c09_end_e
label c092
say kitsune | I'm going east for a while. Someone has to teach foxes to tell the truth. I've started with myself.
label c09_end_e
epilogue C09
label c09_end
if !recruited:C10 c10_end
if q:QC10 c102
say archangel | The host still doesn't answer. I've stopped waiting at the gate. I patrol the harbour instead.
goto c10_end_e
label c102
say archangel | I gave my host its last order back. It's in the archive now, filed under 'kept'. I keep new ones.
label c10_end_e
epilogue C10
label c10_end
if !recruited:C11 c11_end
if q:QC11 c112
say inferna | The ledger is shorter every month. I read the names I've freed out loud, so they hear it.
goto c11_end_e
label c112
say inferna | The Warden's ledger is closed. I carry people now. Upward, only upward.
label c11_end_e
epilogue C11
label c11_end
if !recruited:C12 c12_end
if q:QC12 c122
say corvus | Every cook on the pontoons can brew the cure. I'm down to one patient: me. I'm doing fine.
goto c12_end_e
label c122
say corvus | Idony runs the physic house. She corrects my dosages. Loudly. I've never been happier to be wrong.
label c12_end_e
epilogue C12
label c12_end
if !recruited:C13 c13_end
if q:QC13 c132
say lich | My court is thawing, one throne at a time. It is slow. I have time.
goto c13_end_e
label c132
say lich | The court came home from the Deep. We held a funeral for the mourning. It was very short.
label c13_end_e
epilogue C13
label c13_end
if !recruited:C14 c14_end
if q:QC14 c142
say maldrath | I read the March's names every evening. The graveyards are shorter than the list. Good.
goto c14_end_e
label c142
say maldrath | The First Crown sleeps. I gave its sword back to the tomb. I kept the names.
label c14_end_e
epilogue C14
label c14_end
if !recruited:C15 c15_end
if q:QC15 c152
say velkhar | The dead in the crypts are resting now. The living hold the doors. It works.
goto c15_end_e
label c152
say velkhar | My teacher's gate is shut, and Sorrow has gone home. So have I, mostly.
label c15_end_e
epilogue C15
label c15_end
if !recruited:C16 c16_end
if q:QC16 c162
say kael | My standing orders still exist. I've filed them under 'history'. It's the first order I've given myself.
goto c16_end_e
label c162
say kael | CURATOR's codes are in the public archive. Anyone can cancel an order now. I checked. Twice.
label c16_end_e
epilogue C16
label c16_end
if !recruited:C17 c17_end
if q:QC17 c172
say rider | The roads I patrol are real again. Some of them. I ride the rest anyway.
goto c17_end_e
label c172
say rider | The highway has a name now, and traffic. I hate the traffic. I love the traffic.
label c17_end_e
epilogue C17
label c17_end
if !flag:rescue_all rs_changed
say narr | On the Conduit lift housing, five rescuers' names are carved above the tenders'. The tenders did the carving.
goto rs_end
label rs_changed
if !flag:bound_formed rs_end
say narr | The ones who came back changed sit a little apart at the fire, and are never alone there.
if changed:C07 ch_oni
goto ch_oni_end
label ch_oni
say sable | I don't sleep. I keep watch. Somebody should, and I'm good at it now.
label ch_oni_end
if changed:C04 ch_golem
goto ch_golem_end
label ch_golem
say ivo | CURATOR's joints are better than mine were. I have repainted them anyway. They are mine now.
label ch_golem_end
if changed:C02 ch_morwen
goto ch_morwen_end
label ch_morwen
say tessa | The fragment keeps my lamp lit. I asked it once whose light it was. It said: ours.
label ch_morwen_end
label rs_end
say dain | And me?
say ilyr | And us.
say narr | Raven unpins the old Crown service badge from his coat and leaves it at the public memorial, among the lamps. Then he signs up for a maintenance shift aboard Lanternwake.
epilogue C01
fade out 1.0
music silence
wait 0.8
set dawn
fade in 1.2
music M030
say narr | Dawn over the rebuilt harbor.
objective dain | Lanternwake is waiting at the berth.
@end

@scene CH24_MORNING once
say narr | On the way to the berth, a lamp flickers out.
still ST13_dawn
say worker | Lamp three is out.
say worker | The spare is under the bench.
say dain | Do you need -
say worker | No. Thank you.
say narr | The workers replace the part. The lamp comes back on.
say ilyr | That sound.
say dain | The morning bell.
say ilyr | A door opening.
say dain | Both, then.
objective dain | Step aboard Lanternwake.
@end

@scene CH24_BOARD once
chapter CH24
say narr | Raven steps aboard Lanternwake.
clear_save
credits
ending
@end

@scene T07_LAMP_W
say worker | Morning. Mind the ladder.
@end
